 "discussions": [
  {
   "id": "d_m12",
   "title": "Discussion: Nonviolence: Principle or Strategy?",
   "html": "<div id=\"sparkled-assessment\"><div style=\"background:#231A14; border-bottom:4px solid #6B4A2F; border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:20px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px; color:#E8D3A0; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>DISCUSSION</strong></div><div style=\"font-family:'Archivo Narrow',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:26px; color:#FFFFFF; line-height:1.25; margin-bottom:6px;\">Discussion: Nonviolence: Principle or Strategy?</div><div style=\"font-size:15px; color:#F1E6DA;\">10 points · threaded discussion</div></div><div style=\"border-top:3px double #6B4A2F; margin:0 0 20px;\"></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #2F6B3F; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#2F6B3F; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you start</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Open the lessons \"The Courts and the Boycott\" and \"Direct Action and the Federal Response\". Use My Notebook on those pages to gather your notes and marks, then come back here to post.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #231A14; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#231A14; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>The question</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Many leaders of the civil rights movement chose nonviolence. For Martin Luther King Jr., it was a matter of faith and conscience. Others saw it as a tool that worked because of what the country saw on television. Was nonviolence a principle, a strategy, or both? Your job is to decide which view fits the evidence better.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #6B4A2F; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#6B4A2F; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your post</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Your post (about 100 to 150 words):</strong></p><ol style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 6px; padding-left:22px;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Take a clear position: principle, strategy, or a mix that leans one way.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Give one specific piece of evidence from the lesson \"The Courts and the Boycott\" or the source Brown v. Board of Education that supports you.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Name one fact that cuts against your position, and explain why you still hold it.</li></ol></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #2F6B3F; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#2F6B3F; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your reply</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Your reply (about 50 to 75 words):</strong> Respond to one classmate. Do you agree with their reasoning? If so, strengthen it with something they did not use. If not, say respectfully where their reasoning falls short.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #231A14; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#231A14; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you post</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Post first, then reply. You will not see your classmates' posts until you have posted.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #231A14; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#231A14; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Rubric</strong></div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin-top:6px;\"><tbody><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#F1E6DA; font-size:14px; width:22%;\">Post and reply<br><span style=\"color:#6B4A2F;\">10.0 pts</span></th><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>10.0 pts</strong> Substantive<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Clear position, specific evidence from the week, names a counterpoint, and the reply engages a classmate's actual reasoning</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>6.0 pts</strong> Thin<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Position stated but evidence vague, no counterpoint, or the reply only says \"I agree\"</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>0.0 pts</strong> Missing<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">No post, or no reply</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",
